    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d117">

                <pb facs="0150" n="80" xml:id="pg80"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/4149: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-20T12:00:00-04:00">September 20,
                        1934—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>94. Your 248, September 19, 5 p.m., paragraph 5.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d117-f1"/>
                    You are correct in your assumption that in the event that an inquiry is
                    officially made of you, you may state that the United States will be unable to
                    accept membership on any League commission which may be appointed to deal with
                    the Chaco problem.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
